==English==

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*bʰrewHg-}}
Borrowed into {{inh|en|enm|-}} from {{der|en|fro|fructefier}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈfɹʌktɪfaɪ/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-fructify.wav|a=Southern England}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To [[bear]] [[fruit]]; to generate useful products or ideas.
#* {{RQ:T. Herbert Travaile|chapter=Mohelia, Its Description|page=24|passage=Atop the [Palmito] tree is a pith, in taſte better then Cabbage; and eating it takes avvay the future benefit of grovvth or '''fructifying''', theſe and the Date-tree thriue not, except the male and female be vnited, and haue copulation: the ſhe is only fruitfull.|footer=A noun use.}}
#* {{RQ:Bramah Max Carrados Mysteries|passage=Then one evening early in November Beedel rang Mr Carrados up. The blind man happened to take the call himself, and at the first words he knew that the dull, patient shadowing of weeks was about to '''fructify'''.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1959|month=August|title=Talking of Trains: Reappraisal is completed|journal=Trains Illustrated|page=345|text=It is good to detect hints of a more aggressive attitude from the B.T.C. in face of constant reminders of accumulated deficits and niggling for economies before modernisation schemes have had a chance fully to '''fructify''' {{...}}.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To make [[productive]] or [[fruitful]].

